{"title":"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The Dunbar family consists of a mother, a father, and some children. The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Average\" title=\"Average\">average</a> age of the members of the family is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the father is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5afbad0b221f0ef70186fe70b08e6fc1efdd8dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> years old, and the average age of the mother and children is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. How many children are in the family?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/9/c0904a1807339bc66742fe6716ebc810957bf718.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 2 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 3 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 4 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 5 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"330\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of children. Then the total ages of the family is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/8/9e84a35b21bf6cde90ebfd6266d2d32515a6af8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48 + 16(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" />, and the total number of people in the family is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/6/1f6e3acd481bacb78f324773254902e3a08d848f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />. So\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/e/1be138d16be316ae6222625ea479d7d88a1e76f9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[20 = \\frac{48 + 16(n+1)}{n+2} \\Longrightarrow 20n + 40 = 16n + 64 \\Longrightarrow n = 6\\ \\mathrm{(E)}.\\]\" width=\"478\" height=\"40\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of the children and the mom. The father, who is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5afbad0b221f0ef70186fe70b08e6fc1efdd8dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, plus the sum of the ages of the kids and mom divided by the number of kids and mom plus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (for the dad) = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. This is because the average age of the entire family is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/0/0f06afca5b285202e10a200dc2a833602490ab73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />\nThis statement, written as an equation, is: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/5/1f5ea4671c0efbfd1eaf18e0e06d5bc08cb110ca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{48+16x}{x+1}=20\\]\" width=\"113\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/9/b49dbecea7024b644d54a85d520ef9a3caa83f04.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[48+16x=20x+20\\]\" width=\"161\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/2/47299abfba9d2940ad9ee3ace4ef92ed1df3ca89.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4x=28\\]\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/d/bddb3fa7a8c67bd2de27054bd3cf5f8fa14a9fc3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=7\\]\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> people - <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mom = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> children.\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/2/55206bce678ac0394d97dc04dd72398df2bdf572.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{E}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> be the Mom's age.\n</p><p>Let the number of children be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and their average age be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Their age totaled up is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f79c3676b62fb47243e0d357c87115b6f3395e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>We have the following two equations:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/693235b77d1f848d71d109fa5c473c56f22b9bd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m+48+xy}{2+x}=20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"144\" height=\"39\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/a/9eacfe1d6a2a11904072f3572295a55f993188d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+48+xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"16\" /> is the family's total age and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/b/77b265186f7b5c1c76da9c1bd809a6d0095a7ac4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> is the total number of people in the family.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/693235b77d1f848d71d109fa5c473c56f22b9bd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m+48+xy}{2+x}=20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"144\" height=\"39\" />   \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/d/80dedbca4c85d06a8c71172c096220007d414f75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+48+xy=40+20x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"194\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>The next equation is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/8/f28142c597d714f76003c25ddf8d42cc204ea592.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m+xy}{1+x}=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"104\" height=\"37\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/e/46e24d9865538f2ed50bbcb9d42ed00124971702.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> is the total age of the Mom and the children, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/8/378eec6c0e5607fb907c0c9073d11273c8d69fa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> is the number of children along with the Mom.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/8/f28142c597d714f76003c25ddf8d42cc204ea592.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m+xy}{1+x}=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"104\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/4/f54314b5840a89cf890820d5c38a66a44a97c5b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+xy=16+16x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"151\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>We know the value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/e/46e24d9865538f2ed50bbcb9d42ed00124971702.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />, so we substitute the value back in the first equation.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/d/80dedbca4c85d06a8c71172c096220007d414f75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+48+xy=40+20x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"194\" height=\"17\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/6/75691774a6385f3cf67dfd2966716faaf6f4579a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(16+16x)+48=40+20x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"219\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/9/fd92d02476c3434bf645bf5a3bc249eca83d3c16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Earlier, we set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> to be the number of children. Therefore, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/d/ffd8349ea6d510ab127edb77431f2197ed95a2bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(E)}  6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"45\" height=\"28\" /> children.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A\">2007 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017151912\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.039 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 307/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2322/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 156/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7362/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.922      1 -total\n 60.48%    7.815      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 38.54%    4.980      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6168:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017151912 and revision id 197207. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}